Rodríguez's strategy was to quickly attack Hungary;  ''[[The Guardian]]'' contributor Paul Doyle described El Salvador's tactical scheme as being "monumentally ill-conceived". Only four minutes after the match began, Hungarian captain [[Tibor Nyilasi]] scored. This was followed by an 11th minute goal by [[Gábor Pölöskei]] and a 23rd minute goal by [[László Fazekas]]. Rodríguez made El Salvador's first substitution in the 27th minute, replacing midfielder [[José Luis Rugamas]] with forward [[Luis Ramírez Zapata|Luis Ramírez]] believing that the change could lead to a comeback. While Ramírez and [[Mágico González|Jorge González]] forced Hungarian goalkeeper [[Ferenc Mészáros (footballer, born 1950)|Ferenc Mészáros]] to save a few shots, El Salvador failed to score in the first half{{sfn|Doyle|2018}} that ended with a score of 3–0.{{sfn|Lisi|2007|p=169}} During the halftime break, Hungarian manager [[Kálmán Mészöly]] criticized the Hungarian players for "complacency".{{sfn|Doyle|2018}}

====Second half====
{{multiple image
